import Mathlib
import MassGap.ClayFull

/-!
# MassGap.ObserverAxioms — rotation, OS2 at margin `0`, and density for the observer's `ClayFull` data

`ClayFull.clayFullAt_of_observer` takes, beside the existence-side inputs, invariance of the limit
under `pyth` (`hpyth`), `ClayFull.OS2Zero`, and density of the compact vectors
(`Dense (Set.range X.cvec)`). This module reads each of the three against what the tree proves.

## 1. Density of `Set.range X.cvec` is refuted

`eq_zero_of_dense_real`: in a complex inner product space, a dense set whose pairwise inner products
are real is dense only in the zero space (the closure keeps real inner products, and
`⟪u, i u⟫ = i ‖u‖²`). The compact vectors of every `OSDataSLinked` have real inner products
(`inner_vec`, `vec_compact`), and `OSDataS.nontrivial` gives a non-zero vector, so
`not_dense_range_cvec`: `Set.range X.cvec` is never dense. Hence `not_reconstructs`
(`ClayFull.Reconstructs` is false for every `X`), `not_clayFullAt` (for every `W`, `D`), `not_clayFull`
(`¬ MassGap.ClayFull`), and `not_observerInputs` (the hypothesis of `ClayFull.clayFull_of_observer`
cannot be supplied). The density a reconstruction carries is that of the complex span.

`ReconstructsSpan` is `ClayFull.Reconstructs` with `Dense (span ℂ (range X.cvec))`, and
`ClayFullAtSpan` is `ClayFull.ClayFullAt` with `ReconstructsSpan` in place of `Reconstructs`.

* `dense_span_gvecT`: the complex span of the vectors of all compact margin monomials is dense in
  `ContinuumTimeGroup.FlowH` (a vector orthogonal to them is orthogonal to the pre-Hilbert space,
  `ContinuumTimeGroup.inner_pre_eq_zero`, which is dense in its completion).
* `dense_span_of_cyclic`: a span is dense when every vector of a set with dense span lies in its
  closure. `CyclicD`: every compact margin monomial's vector lies in the closed span of the vectors of
  the monomials with fields in `D`. `dense_span_cvec_of_cyclic`: `CyclicD` gives the density clause
  for the observer. `CyclicD` is a cyclicity statement for the class `D` inside the space of all local
  fields; nothing in the tree supplies it, and it holds at `D = Set.univ` by `dense_span_gvecT`.

## 2. OS2 at margin `0`

`OS2Zero` reads only `X.SM = schwSFM`, which does not depend on the margin `r` of `X`.
`exists_margin_pos`: a finite set of margin-`0` monomials has a common margin `r' > 0`.
`gram_zero_of_pos`: reflection positivity of a kernel at every margin `r' > 0` gives it at margin
`0`. `os2Zero_of_physRange_all`: if the observer's flow has physical range `r'` for every `r' > 0`,
`OS2Zero` holds (`ObserverOSEuclidS.schwSFM_gram_nonneg` at each `r'`).
`physRange_all_of_reach`: that is the case when `aₖ · range k → 0`, and `reach_tendsto_of_bounded`
when the lattice range is bounded (`obsConfFlow_reach_tendsto`: the `SU(2)` APE observer at a bounded
box radius). For a flow whose lattice range grows like `r / aₖ`, the physical range does not shrink
and `OS2Zero` is a statement beyond the flow's reach: the flowed fields at times below `r` are
smeared across the reflection plane. A bounded lattice range keeps the flowed plaquette mean at its
bare size, while the moment inputs (E) ask it to vanish like `aₖ⁴`
(`ObserverMoments.not_classMoments_of_mean_ge`); the two are not expected together (argued, not
proved here).

`localLink_gram_nonneg`: `ClayFull.LocalLink` gives reflection positivity at margin `0` for the local
composite, on separated positive-time monomials of every positive separation
(`⟪w P, w Q⟫ = S_Z(θP ∪ Q)`, so the Gram sum is `‖∑ c_P w P‖²`).

## 3. `pyth`

`ObserverSymField.observerSO4_symPlaq` reduces `SO(4)` to `pyth`; orbit continuity
(`ObserverRotationDense.orbitContinuous_energy0`) and density of the group generated by `pyth` and the
signed permutations (`SO4Planes`) are proved. `contSF_rot_eq_iff`: under the uniform bound, a rotation
leaves the flowed limit unchanged exactly when the lattice readings of the rotated and unrotated
families differ by a sequence tending to `0` along `ultra`. `PythLatticeFlow` is that for `pyth` on
`SymPlaqClass`, and `hpyth_iff_lattice` identifies it with the `hpyth` input. It is the statement that
the rotation-breaking part of the lattice readings vanishes in the limit, at every smeared family;
no lattice identity carries `pyth` (`ObserverRotation.pyth_not_lattice`).

## 4. The observer's statement

`clayFullAtSpan_of_observer`: `ClayFullAtSpan` for the observer from the existence-side inputs of
`ClayFull.clayFullAt_of_observer`, with `PythLatticeFlow`, `aₖ · range k → 0`, `CyclicD`,
`NonGaussian` and `LocalLink` as inputs. `ClayFull.lean` is not changed here: `ClayFull`,
`ClayFullAt`, `Reconstructs`, `ObserverInputs` and `clayFullAt_of_observer` keep the range-density
clause, which section 1 refutes.

DERIVED (module-wide): `0` the zero vector, the sign, the margin and the limit; `1` the margin of the
empty set; `2` the halving of a margin; `4` in `Fin 4` the spacetime dimension; `3` the APE box
overhang of `ObserverFlow.obsConfFlow`.
-/

noncomputable section

namespace MassGap.ObserverAxioms

open MassGap MassGap.InfiniteLattice MassGap.ContinuumField MassGap.ContinuumSchwinger
  MassGap.ContinuumFlow MassGap.ContinuumHypercubic MassGap.ObserverOS MassGap.ObserverOSGrowth
  MassGap.ObserverOSSchwartz MassGap.ObserverOSTempered MassGap.ObserverEnergyBox
  MassGap.ObserverOSEuclidS MassGap.ObserverOSReconstructionS MassGap.ObserverOSLinked
  MassGap.ObserverRotation MassGap.ObserverSymField MassGap.ContinuumTimeGroup MassGap.ClayFull
  Filter
open scoped Topology Matrix

variable {N : ℕ}

/-! ## 1. Density -/

section Density

/-- **A dense set with real inner products lives in the zero space.** The closure keeps real inner
products, and `⟪u, i u⟫ = i ‖u‖²`.

DERIVED: `0` the imaginary part and the zero vector; `2` the square of the norm. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_dense_real {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℂ E] {S : Set E}
    (hS : ∀ u ∈ S, ∀ v ∈ S, (inner ℂ u v).im = 0) (hd : Dense S) (u : E) : u = 0 := by
  have hcl : ∀ u v : E, (inner ℂ u v).im = 0 := by
    have hc : IsClosed {p : E × E | (inner ℂ p.1 p.2).im = 0} :=
      isClosed_eq (Complex.continuous_im.comp (continuous_fst.inner continuous_snd))
        continuous_const
    have hsub : closure (S ×ˢ S) ⊆ {p : E × E | (inner ℂ p.1 p.2).im = 0} :=
      hc.closure_subset_iff.mpr (fun p hp => hS p.1 hp.1 p.2 hp.2)
    intro u v
    exact hsub ((hd.prod hd) (u, v))
  have h := hcl u (Complex.I • u)
  rw [inner_smul_right, Complex.mul_im, Complex.I_re, Complex.I_im, zero_mul, zero_add,
    one_mul] at h
  have h2 : ‖u‖ ^ 2 = 0 := (inner_self_eq_norm_sq (𝕜 := ℂ) u).symm.trans h
  exact norm_eq_zero.mp (pow_eq_zero_iff (n := 2) (by norm_num) |>.mp h2)

#print axioms eq_zero_of_dense_real

variable {D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N))} {τ : Fin 4} {r : ℝ}

/-- **The compact vectors are never dense**: their inner products are real, and the space has a
non-zero vector.

DERIVED: `0` the imaginary part of a real number. -/
theorem not_dense_range_cvec (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) : ¬ Dense (Set.range X.cvec) := by
  intro hd
  have hS : ∀ u ∈ Set.range X.cvec, ∀ v ∈ Set.range X.cvec, (inner ℂ u v).im = 0 := by
    rintro _ ⟨P, rfl⟩ _ ⟨Q, rfl⟩
    rw [← X.vec_compact P, ← X.vec_compact Q, X.inner_vec]
    exact Complex.ofReal_im _
  obtain ⟨u, -, hu⟩ := X.base.nontrivial
  exact hu (eq_zero_of_dense_real hS hd u)

#print axioms not_dense_range_cvec

/-- **`ClayFull.Reconstructs` is false for every linked datum.**

DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem not_reconstructs (hN : N ≠ 0) (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) : ¬ Reconstructs hN X :=
  fun h => not_dense_range_cvec X h.2.2

#print axioms not_reconstructs

/-- **`ClayFull.ClayFullAt` is false at every construction.**

DERIVED: `4` in `Fin 4` the dimension. -/
theorem not_clayFullAt (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N) (D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)))
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D) :
    ¬ ClayFullAt hN W D hD := by
  rintro ⟨τ, r, X, -, -, -, -, -, -, -, -, hR, -⟩
  exact not_reconstructs hN X hR

#print axioms not_clayFullAt

/-- **`MassGap.ClayFull` as stated is refuted** (at `N = 2`).

DERIVED: `2` the least colour count. -/
theorem not_clayFull : ¬ MassGap.ClayFull := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨hN, W, D, hD, hC⟩ := h 2 le_rfl
  exact not_clayFullAt hN W D hD hC

#print axioms not_clayFull

/-- **The hypothesis of `ClayFull.clayFull_of_observer` cannot be supplied.**

DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem not_observerInputs (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N) : ¬ ObserverInputs hN W := by
  rintro ⟨hW, hcube, t, C, ht, hC0, hU, O, hO, h, τ, r, hphys, m0, L, hL, ρ, hρ0, hρ1, hg, hNT,
    -, -, -, -, hdense⟩
  exact not_dense_range_cvec _ hdense

#print axioms not_observerInputs

/-- **The reconstruction is the one of `X.SM`**, with the density of a reconstruction: the vacuum is
the empty monomial's vector, the dyadic shift acts as `X.base.time a_m`, and the complex span of the
compact vectors is dense.

DERIVED: `0` the empty monomial's length. -/
def ReconstructsSpan (hN : N ≠ 0) (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) : Prop :=
  X.base.vac = X.cvec ⟨emptyMargin N τ r, fun i => i.elim0⟩
    ∧ (∀ (m : ℕ) (Q : MarginMonoD N D τ r),
        X.cvec ⟨MarginMono.shift hN τ m Q.1, fun i => Q.2 i⟩
          = X.base.time (dySpacing N m) (X.cvec Q))
    ∧ Dense (Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range X.cvec) : Set X.base.H)

/-- **A span is dense when a set with dense span lies in its closure.**

DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem dense_span_of_cyclic {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℂ E]
    {S T : Set E} (hT : Dense (Submodule.span ℂ T : Set E))
    (hc : ∀ x ∈ T, x ∈ (Submodule.span ℂ S).topologicalClosure) :
    Dense (Submodule.span ℂ S : Set E) := by
  rw [Submodule.dense_iff_topologicalClosure_eq_top] at hT ⊢
  refine top_unique ?_
  rw [← hT]
  exact Submodule.topologicalClosure_minimal _ (Submodule.span_le.mpr hc)
    (Submodule.isClosed_topologicalClosure _)

#print axioms dense_span_of_cyclic

/-- **The compact vectors span a dense subspace of the flowed space**: a vector orthogonal to every
`gvecT Q` is orthogonal to the pre-Hilbert space, which is dense.

DERIVED: `0` the zero vector. -/
theorem dense_span_gvecT (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φ : Flow N) (hB : UniformBoundF hN Φ) (τ : Fin 4) {r : ℝ}
    (hpos : Φ.PosPreserving τ r) :
    Dense (Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range (gvecT hN Φ hB τ hpos)) : Set (FlowH hN Φ hB τ hpos)) := by
  rw [Submodule.dense_iff_topologicalClosure_eq_top, Submodule.topologicalClosure_eq_top_iff,
    Submodule.eq_bot_iff]
  intro x hx
  have horth : ∀ Q : MarginMono N τ r, inner ℂ x (gvecT hN Φ hB τ hpos Q) = 0 := fun Q =>
    (Submodule.mem_orthogonal' _ x).mp hx _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨Q, rfl⟩)
  have hall : ∀ y : FlowH hN Φ hB τ hpos, inner ℂ x y = 0 := fun y =>
    UniformSpace.Completion.induction_on y
      (isClosed_eq (continuous_const.inner continuous_id) continuous_const)
      (inner_pre_eq_zero hN Φ hB τ hpos x horth)
  exact inner_self_eq_zero.mp (hall x)

#print axioms dense_span_gvecT

/-- **Cyclicity of the class `D`**: every compact margin monomial's vector lies in the closed complex
span of the vectors of the compact margin monomials with fields in `D`.

DERIVED: `4` in `Fin 4` the dimension. -/
def CyclicD (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N) {D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N))}
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (hpos : ∀ O ∈ D, ∀ U, 0 ≤ O.1 U) (hcube : ∀ O ∈ D, CubeMomentBound hN W O) (τ : Fin 4)
    {r : ℝ} (hphys : (energy0 W D hD).PhysRange r) : Prop :=
  ∀ Q : MarginMono N τ r,
    gvecT hN (energy0 W D hD) (uniformBoundF_energy0 hN W D hD hpos hcube) τ
        (Flow.posPreserving_of_physRange hN (energy0 W D hD) hphys τ) Q
      ∈ (Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range (fun Q' : MarginMonoD N D τ r =>
          gvecT hN (energy0 W D hD) (uniformBoundF_energy0 hN W D hD hpos hcube) τ
            (Flow.posPreserving_of_physRange hN (energy0 W D hD) hphys τ) Q'.1))).topologicalClosure

/-- **The density clause for the observer from cyclicity of `D`.**

DERIVED: `4` in `Fin 4` the dimension. -/
theorem dense_span_cvec_of_cyclic (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N) {D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N))}
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (hpos : ∀ O ∈ D, ∀ U, 0 ≤ O.1 U) (hcube : ∀ O ∈ D, CubeMomentBound hN W O) (τ : Fin 4)
    {r : ℝ} (hphys : (energy0 W D hD).PhysRange r) (hcyc : CyclicD hN W hD hpos hcube τ hphys) :
    Dense (Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range (fun Q' : MarginMonoD N D τ r =>
          gvecT hN (energy0 W D hD) (uniformBoundF_energy0 hN W D hD hpos hcube) τ
            (Flow.posPreserving_of_physRange hN (energy0 W D hD) hphys τ) Q'.1))
      : Set (FlowH hN (energy0 W D hD) (uniformBoundF_energy0 hN W D hD hpos hcube) τ
          (Flow.posPreserving_of_physRange hN (energy0 W D hD) hphys τ))) :=
  dense_span_of_cyclic (dense_span_gvecT hN _ _ τ _) (by rintro _ ⟨Q, rfl⟩; exact hcyc Q)

#print axioms dense_span_cvec_of_cyclic

end Density

/-! ## 2. OS2 at margin `0` -/

section Margin

/-- **A finite set of margin-`0` monomials has a common positive margin.**

DERIVED: `0` the margin; `1` the margin of the empty set; `2` the halving. -/
theorem exists_margin_pos {τ : Fin 4} (s : Finset (DMarginMono N τ 0)) :
    ∃ r' : ℝ, 0 < r' ∧ ∀ P ∈ s, ∃ d : ℝ, 0 < d ∧ r' < d ∧ posAtD τ d P.1 := by
  classical
  refine Finset.induction_on s ⟨1, one_pos, fun P hP => by simp at hP⟩ ?_
  intro P s _ ih
  obtain ⟨r', hr', h⟩ := ih
  obtain ⟨d, hd, -, hPd⟩ := P.2
  refine ⟨min r' (d / 2), lt_min hr' (half_pos hd), fun Q hQ => ?_⟩
  rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp hQ with rfl | hQ
  · exact ⟨d, hd, (min_le_right _ _).trans_lt (half_lt_self hd), hPd⟩
  · obtain ⟨e, he, hre, hQe⟩ := h Q hQ
    exact ⟨e, he, (min_le_left _ _).trans_lt hre, hQe⟩

#print axioms exists_margin_pos

/-- **Positivity at every positive margin gives positivity at margin `0`.** A finite set of
margin-`0` monomials is a set of margin-`r'` monomials for some `r' > 0`.

DERIVED: `0` the margin and the sign. -/
theorem gram_zero_of_pos {τ : Fin 4} (K : DMono N → DMono N → ℝ) (A : DMono N → Prop)
    (h : ∀ r' : ℝ, 0 < r' → ∀ s : Finset (DMarginMono N τ r'), (∀ P ∈ s, A P.1) →
      ∀ c : DMarginMono N τ r' → ℝ, 0 ≤ ∑ P ∈ s, ∑ Q ∈ s, c P * c Q * K P.1 Q.1)
    (s : Finset (DMarginMono N τ 0)) (hs : ∀ P ∈ s, A P.1) (c : DMarginMono N τ 0 → ℝ) :
    0 ≤ ∑ P ∈ s, ∑ Q ∈ s, c P * c Q * K P.1 Q.1 := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨r', hr', hm⟩ := exists_margin_pos s
  let ι : DMarginMono N τ r' → DMarginMono N τ 0 := fun P =>
    ⟨P.1, by obtain ⟨d, hd, -, hP⟩ := P.2; exact ⟨d, hd, hd, hP⟩⟩
  have hinj : Function.Injective ι := fun P Q hPQ =>
    Subtype.ext (congrArg (fun x : DMarginMono N τ 0 => x.1) hPQ)
  let lift : {P // P ∈ s} → DMarginMono N τ r' := fun P => ⟨P.1.1, hm P.1 P.2⟩
  set s' : Finset (DMarginMono N τ r') := s.attach.image lift with hs'
  have himg : s'.image ι = s := by
    rw [hs', Finset.image_image]
    have e : ι ∘ lift = Subtype.val := funext fun P => Subtype.ext rfl
    rw [e, Finset.attach_image_val]
  have hs'A : ∀ P ∈ s', A P.1 := by
    intro P hP
    have hP' : ι P ∈ s := himg ▸ Finset.mem_image_of_mem ι hP
    exact hs (ι P) hP'
  have key := h r' hr' s' hs'A (fun P => c (ι P))
  rw [← himg, Finset.sum_image (fun x _ y _ hxy => hinj hxy)]
  have e : ∀ P ∈ s', ∑ Q ∈ s'.image ι, c (ι P) * c Q * K (ι P).1 Q.1
      = ∑ Q ∈ s', c (ι P) * c (ι Q) * K P.1 Q.1 := fun P _ =>
    Finset.sum_image (fun x _ y _ hxy => hinj hxy)
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl e]
  exact key

#print axioms gram_zero_of_pos

/-- **`OS2Zero` for the observer from physical range at every positive margin.**

DERIVED: `0` the margin; `1` the top of `ρ`; `4` in `Fin 4` the dimension. -/
theorem os2Zero_of_physRange_all (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N) {D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N))}
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (hpos : ∀ O ∈ D, ∀ U, 0 ≤ O.1 U) (hcube : ∀ O ∈ D, CubeMomentBound hN W O) {t C : ℝ}
    (ht : 0 < t) (hC0 : 0 ≤ C) (hU : ClassMoments hN W D t C)
    {O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)} (hO : O ∈ D) (h : UnitCubeExpBound hN W O) (τ : Fin 4)
    {r : ℝ} (hphys : (energy0 W D hD).PhysRange r) (m0 : ℕ) {L : ℝ} (hL : 0 < L) {ρ : ℝ}
    (hρ0 : 0 < ρ) (hρ1 : ρ < 1)
    (hg : TransferGap.GapAt (ObserverEnergyReductionsN.transferN hN (energy0 W D hD)
      (uniformBoundF_energy0 hN W D hD hpos hcube) τ hphys m0) ρ)
    (hNT : FlowConnectedNonzero hN (energy0 W D hD) τ r)
    (hall : ∀ r' : ℝ, 0 < r' → (energy0 W D hD).PhysRange r') :
    OS2Zero (observerOSDataSLinked hN W hD hpos hcube ht hC0 hU hO h τ hphys m0 hL hρ0 hρ1 hg hNT) := by
  intro s hs c
  exact gram_zero_of_pos (kernS hN W D hD τ) (fun P => ∀ i, (P.2 i).1 ∈ D)
    (fun r' hr' s' hs' c' => schwSFM_gram_nonneg hN W hD hpos hcube ht hC0 hU τ (hall r' hr') s' hs' c')
    s hs c

#print axioms os2Zero_of_physRange_all

/-- **Physical range at every positive margin from a vanishing physical reach** `aₖ · range k → 0`.

DERIVED: `0` the limit and the sign. -/
theorem physRange_all_of_reach (W : ConfFlow N) (D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)))
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (hreach : Tendsto (fun k => dySpacing N k * (W.range k : ℝ)) atTop (𝓝 0)) :
    ∀ r' : ℝ, 0 < r' → (energy0 W D hD).PhysRange r' :=
  fun _ hr' => hreach.eventually (eventually_le_nhds hr')

#print axioms physRange_all_of_reach

/-- **A bounded lattice range has vanishing physical reach.**

DERIVED: `0` the limit and the sign. -/
theorem reach_tendsto_of_bounded (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N) {R0 : ℕ} (hR : ∀ k, W.range k ≤ R0) :
    Tendsto (fun k => dySpacing N k * (W.range k : ℝ)) atTop (𝓝 0) := by
  have h0 : Tendsto (fun k => dySpacing N k * (R0 : ℝ)) atTop (𝓝 0) := by
    simpa using (tendsto_dySpacing N).mul_const (R0 : ℝ)
  exact squeeze_zero
    (fun k => mul_nonneg (dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) k).le (Nat.cast_nonneg _))
    (fun k => mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (Nat.cast_le.mpr (hR k))
      (dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) k).le) h0

#print axioms reach_tendsto_of_bounded

/-- **The `SU(2)` APE observer at a bounded box radius has vanishing physical reach.**

DERIVED: `3` the box overhang of `obsConfFlow`; `1/6` the dominance bound. -/
theorem obsConfFlow_reach_tendsto {c : ℝ} (hc0 : 0 ≤ c) (hc : c < 1 / 6) (n R : ℕ → ℕ) {R0 : ℕ}
    (hR : ∀ k, R k ≤ R0) :
    Tendsto (fun k => dySpacing 2 k * ((ObserverFlow.obsConfFlow c hc0 hc n R).range k : ℝ))
      atTop (𝓝 0) :=
  reach_tendsto_of_bounded ObserverClay.two_ne _ (R0 := R0 + 3)
    (fun k => Nat.add_le_add_right (hR k) 3)

#print axioms obsConfFlow_reach_tendsto

/-- **`LocalLink` carries reflection positivity of the local composite at margin `0`**: on separated
positive-time monomials of every positive separation, `∑ c_P c_Q S_Z(θP ∪ Q) = ‖∑ c_P w P‖² ≥ 0`.

DERIVED: `0` the sign; `4` in `Fin 4` the dimension. -/
theorem localLink_gram_nonneg (hN : N ≠ 0) {D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N))} {τ : Fin 4} {r : ℝ}
    (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r) (hLL : LocalLink hN X) :
    ∃ Z : ℕ → LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N) → ℝ, ∀ (s : Finset (ContinuumSep.SepMono N τ))
      (c : ContinuumSep.SepMono N τ → ℝ),
        0 ≤ ∑ P ∈ s, ∑ Q ∈ s, c P * c Q * ContinuumSep.kernSep hN (Renorm.connected hN Z) τ P Q := by
  obtain ⟨Z, G, w, hin, -⟩ := hLL
  refine ⟨Z, fun s c => ?_⟩
  set v : X.base.H := ∑ P ∈ s, (c P : ℂ) • w P with hv
  have e : inner ℂ v v = ((∑ P ∈ s, ∑ Q ∈ s,
      c P * c Q * ContinuumSep.kernSep hN (Renorm.connected hN Z) τ P Q : ℝ) : ℂ) := by
    simp only [hv, sum_inner, inner_sum, inner_smul_left, inner_smul_right, hin,
      Complex.conj_ofReal]
    push_cast
    simp only [Finset.mul_sum]
    rw [Finset.sum_comm]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun P _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl fun Q _ => by ring
  have h0 := inner_self_nonneg (𝕜 := ℂ) (x := v)
  rw [e] at h0
  simpa using h0

#print axioms localLink_gram_nonneg

end Margin

/-! ## 3. `pyth` -/

section Pyth

/-- **A rotation of the flowed limit in lattice form**: under the uniform bound both readings converge
along `ultra`, so the limits agree exactly when the difference of the readings tends to `0`.

DERIVED: `0` the limit. -/
theorem contSF_rot_eq_iff (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φ : Flow N) (hB : UniformBoundF hN Φ)
    (A : Matrix (Fin 4) (Fin 4) ℝ) {ι : Type} [Fintype ι] (F : ι → SField N) :
    contSF hN Φ (rotFam A F) = contSF hN Φ F ↔
      Tendsto (fun k => latSF hN Φ k (rotFam A F) - latSF hN Φ k F) (ultra : Filter ℕ) (𝓝 0) := by
  haveI : ((ultra : Ultrafilter ℕ) : Filter ℕ).NeBot := ultra.neBot'
  have hlim := (tendsto_contSF hN Φ hB (rotFam A F)).sub (tendsto_contSF hN Φ hB F)
  constructor
  · intro h
    rw [h, sub_self] at hlim
    exact hlim
  · intro h
    exact sub_eq_zero.mp (tendsto_nhds_unique hlim h)

#print axioms contSF_rot_eq_iff

/-- **(P) in lattice form for the observer**: at every family of hypercubic scalars of
`SymPlaqClass` with uniformly continuous test functions, the lattice readings of the `pyth`-rotated
family and of the family differ by a sequence tending to `0` along `ultra`.

DERIVED: `0` the limit; `4` in `Fin 4` the dimension. -/
def PythLatticeFlow (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N) : Prop :=
  ∀ (ι : Type) [Fintype ι] (F : ι → SField N),
    (∀ i, (F i).1 ∈ SymPlaqClass N ∧ HypScalar (F i).1) → (∀ i, UniformContinuous (F i).2.1) →
      Tendsto (fun k => latSF hN (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)) k (rotFam pyth F)
        - latSF hN (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)) k F) (ultra : Filter ℕ) (𝓝 0)

/-- **The `hpyth` input is `PythLatticeFlow`.**

DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem hpyth_iff_lattice (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N)
    (hW : ∀ (k : ℕ) (e : Equiv.Perm (Fin 4)) (U : Cfg N), W.V k (iaxisConf e U) = iaxisConf e (W.V k U))
    (hcube : ∀ O ∈ PlaqClass N, CubeMomentBound hN W O) :
    (∀ (ι : Type) [Fintype ι] (F : ι → SField N),
      (∀ i, (F i).1 ∈ SymPlaqClass N ∧ HypScalar (F i).1) → (∀ i, UniformContinuous (F i).2.1) →
        contSF hN (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)) (rotFam pyth F)
          = contSF hN (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)) F) ↔ PythLatticeFlow hN W := by
  have hB := uniformBoundF_energy0 hN W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N) (symPlaq_nonneg hN)
    (symPlaq_cube hN W hW hcube)
  constructor
  · intro h ι _ F hF hUc
    exact (contSF_rot_eq_iff hN _ hB pyth F).mp (h ι F hF hUc)
  · intro h ι _ F hF hUc
    exact (contSF_rot_eq_iff hN _ hB pyth F).mpr (h ι F hF hUc)

#print axioms hpyth_iff_lattice

/-- **`PythLatticeFlow` from the same statement along `atTop`.**

DERIVED: `0` the limit. -/
theorem pythLatticeFlow_of_atTop (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N)
    (h : ∀ (ι : Type) [Fintype ι] (F : ι → SField N),
      (∀ i, (F i).1 ∈ SymPlaqClass N ∧ HypScalar (F i).1) → (∀ i, UniformContinuous (F i).2.1) →
        Tendsto (fun k => latSF hN (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)) k (rotFam pyth F)
          - latSF hN (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)) k F) atTop (𝓝 0)) :
    PythLatticeFlow hN W :=
  fun ι _ F hF hUc => (h ι F hF hUc).mono_left ultra_le

#print axioms pythLatticeFlow_of_atTop

end Pyth

/-! ## 4. The observer's statement -/

section Capstone

/-- **The Clay statement at one construction with the density of a reconstruction**: `ClayFullAt`
with `ReconstructsSpan` in place of `Reconstructs`.

DERIVED: `4` in `Fin 4` is the spacetime dimension. -/
def ClayFullAtSpan (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N) (D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)))
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D) : Prop :=
  ∃ (τ : Fin 4) (r : ℝ) (X : OSDataSLinked N D τ r),
    (∀ (ι : Type) [Fintype ι] (O : ι → LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)) (g : ι → Decaying),
        X.SM O g = schwSFM hN W D hD O g)
      ∧ X.O ∈ D ∧ HypScalar X.O
      ∧ TranslationInv X ∧ RotationInv X ∧ ReflectionInv X ∧ OS2 X ∧ OS2Zero X
      ∧ ReconstructsSpan hN X ∧ HamiltonianGap X.base ∧ NonGaussian X ∧ LocalLink hN X

/-- **`ClayFullAtSpan` for the observer.** The existence-side inputs of
`ClayFull.clayFullAt_of_observer`; `PythLatticeFlow` for `pyth`; vanishing physical reach
`aₖ · range k → 0` for `OS2Zero`; `CyclicD` for the density; `NonGaussian` and `LocalLink`.

DERIVED: `0` the signs and the excluded colour count; `1` the top of `ρ`; `4` in `Fin 4` the
dimension. -/
theorem clayFullAtSpan_of_observer (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N)
    (hW : ∀ (k : ℕ) (e : Equiv.Perm (Fin 4)) (U : Cfg N), W.V k (iaxisConf e U) = iaxisConf e (W.V k U))
    (hcube : ∀ O ∈ PlaqClass N, CubeMomentBound hN W O) {t C : ℝ} (ht : 0 < t) (hC0 : 0 ≤ C)
    (hU : ClassMoments hN W (SymPlaqClass N) t C)
    {O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)} (hO : O ∈ SymPlaqClass N) (h : UnitCubeExpBound hN W O)
    (τ : Fin 4) {r : ℝ} (hphys : (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)).PhysRange r)
    (m0 : ℕ) {L : ℝ} (hL : 0 < L) {ρ : ℝ} (hρ0 : 0 < ρ) (hρ1 : ρ < 1)
    (hg : TransferGap.GapAt (ObserverEnergyReductionsN.transferN hN
      (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N))
      (uniformBoundF_energy0 hN W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N) (symPlaq_nonneg hN)
        (symPlaq_cube hN W hW hcube)) τ hphys m0) ρ)
    (hNT : FlowConnectedNonzero hN (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)) τ r)
    (hpythL : PythLatticeFlow hN W)
    (hreach : Tendsto (fun k => dySpacing N k * (W.range k : ℝ)) atTop (𝓝 0))
    (hcyc : CyclicD hN W (symPlaq_refl N) (symPlaq_nonneg hN) (symPlaq_cube hN W hW hcube) τ hphys)
    (hNG : NonGaussian (observerOSDataSLinked hN W (symPlaq_refl N) (symPlaq_nonneg hN)
      (symPlaq_cube hN W hW hcube) ht hC0 hU hO h τ hphys m0 hL hρ0 hρ1 hg hNT))
    (hLL : LocalLink hN (observerOSDataSLinked hN W (symPlaq_refl N) (symPlaq_nonneg hN)
      (symPlaq_cube hN W hW hcube) ht hC0 hU hO h τ hphys m0 hL hρ0 hρ1 hg hNT)) :
    ClayFullAtSpan hN W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N) := by
  have hcubeS := symPlaq_cube hN W hW hcube
  have hpyth := (hpyth_iff_lattice hN W hW hcube).mpr hpythL
  have hSO4 := observerSO4_symPlaq hN W hW hcube hpyth
  have hB := uniformBoundF_energy0 hN W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N) (symPlaq_nonneg hN) hcubeS
  refine ⟨τ, r, observerOSDataSLinked hN W (symPlaq_refl N) (symPlaq_nonneg hN) hcubeS ht hC0 hU hO
    h τ hphys m0 hL hρ0 hρ1 hg hNT, fun ι _ O' g => rfl, hO, symPlaq_hypScalar O hO, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_,
    os2Zero_of_physRange_all hN W (symPlaq_refl N) (symPlaq_nonneg hN) hcubeS ht hC0 hU hO h τ
      hphys m0 hL hρ0 hρ1 hg hNT (physRange_all_of_reach W _ (symPlaq_refl N) hreach),
    ⟨rfl, ?_, dense_span_cvec_of_cyclic hN W (symPlaq_refl N) (symPlaq_nonneg hN) hcubeS τ hphys
      hcyc⟩, ?_, hNG, hLL⟩
  · intro ι _ O' hO' g hg' v
    exact schwSFM_translate hN W (symPlaq_refl N) (symPlaq_nonneg hN) hcubeS ht hC0 hU O' hO' g hg' v
  · intro A hA ι _ O' hO' g hg'
    exact schwSFM_rotate hN W (symPlaq_refl N) (symPlaq_nonneg hN) ht hC0 hU hSO4 hA O'
      (fun i => (hO' i).1) (fun i => hO' i) g hg'
  · intro σ ι _ O' hO' g
    exact schwSFM_reflect hN W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N) σ O' (fun i => (hO' i).2.2 σ) g
  · intro s hs c
    exact schwSFM_gram_nonneg hN W (symPlaq_refl N) (symPlaq_nonneg hN) hcubeS ht hC0 hU τ hphys s hs c
  · intro m Q
    have hpp := Flow.posPreserving_of_physRange hN (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)) hphys τ
    have h1 := timeT_dyadic hN (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)) hB τ hpp m 1
    rw [Nat.cast_one, one_mul, pow_one] at h1
    show gvecT hN (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)) hB τ hpp (MarginMono.shift hN τ m Q.1)
      = timeT hN (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)) hB τ hpp (dySpacing N m)
          (gvecT hN (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)) hB τ hpp Q.1)
    rw [h1, stepT_gvecT]
  · exact hamiltonianGap_of_selfAdjoint _
      (observer_generator_isSelfAdjoint hN (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)) hB τ
        (Flow.posPreserving_of_physRange hN (energy0 W (SymPlaqClass N) (symPlaq_refl N)) hphys τ))

#print axioms clayFullAtSpan_of_observer

end Capstone

